  ],
  "text": "One animal deals with old age by turning back into a baby. Then doing it again. Every other life runs one way. Born, grow, wear out, done. Turritopsis dohrnii is a jellyfish about the size of your fingernail. When it is starving or badly injured, it does not die. It sinks and collapses into a lump. Then its adult cells do something almost nothing else alive can manage. They turn into completely different cell types, and the lump rebuilds itself as the juvenile stage. And nobody has found a limit on how many times it can do this. It is not the only one cheating the clock. Greenland sharks pass four hundred years. But none of them are unkillable. Almost all get eaten. They just never die of being old. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
